    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1002">

                <pb facs="1159" n="963" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg963"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 (Potsdam)/7–3145</note>
                <head>No. 1002<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The United States
                            Representatives on the Economic Subcommittee to the Secretary of State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d1002-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1002-f2"/>]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-08-01T13:00:00+03:00">August 1 [1945]—1:00
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Report to the Secretary on the
                        Work of the Economic Subcommittee</hi></p>
                <p>There is attached the Third Report of the Economic Subcommittee to the Foreign
                    Ministers.</p>
                <p>With respect to the question of German external assets, the U. S. and U. K. recommended the inclusion in the Economic
                        Principles<anchor n="3" xml:id="d1002-f3"/> of the following: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“18. Appropriate steps shall be taken by the Control Council to exercise
                            control and the power of disposition over German owned <pb facs="1160"
                                n="964" xml:id="pg964"/> external assets not already under the
                            control of United Nations which have taken part in the war against Germany.”</p></quote></p>
                <p rendition="#flush">We also recommended that appropriate reference to this matter
                    be made in the communiqué.</p>
                <p>The Soviet representatives, while stating that they had very little interest in
                    the matter, reserved their position pending a study of the entire problem.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>


                <xi:include href="d1002-a1.xml" xpointer="d1002-a1"/>
            </div>
